# Dependencies and builds
node_modules/
.next/
coverage/

# Generated by Next on every `next dev` / `next build` / `next typegen`, and
# NOT stable between them: dev writes `.next/dev/types`, build writes
# `.next/types`, so whichever variant is committed is wrong half the time and
# the file shows up dirty after every dev run. It kept turning up staged
# alongside unrelated work for exactly that reason.
#
# Safe to ignore because nothing consumes the committed copy:
#   - CI runs `npx next typegen` before `npx tsc --noEmit` (ci.yml), which
#     writes the build variant first;
#   - `next build` regenerates it, so Vercel is unaffected;
#   - `tsconfig.json` already includes BOTH `.next/types/**` and
#     `.next/dev/types/**`, so the type paths are mode-agnostic already;
#   - `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with the file absent and no `.next` present
#     (verified on a clean tree), so a fresh clone typechecks before anyone
#     runs a Next command.
# The file itself says "This file should not be edited", which is the other
# half of the argument: it is a build artifact, not source.
next-env.d.ts

