# Cursor: track rules, skills, hooks, memories, and the plugin settings so
# they ship with the repo. Everything else under .cursor/ stays local.
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/
!.cursor/rules/**
!.cursor/skills/
!.cursor/skills/**
!.cursor/hooks/
!.cursor/hooks/**
!.cursor/hooks.json
!.cursor/settings.json
!.cursor/memory/
!.cursor/memory/**
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
# .claude/ stays tracked for Claude Code: permission allowlist, SessionStart
# hook, and thin skill wrappers that point at .cursor/skills/. Only the
# per-machine overrides stay out.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Private planning docs
PRDs/geminiChat.md

# Supabase CLI temp files (auto-generated by `supabase link`, contain infra secrets)
supabase/.temp/
# NOTE: supabase/config.toml is now TRACKED: it pins verify_jwt per edge
# function and CI's bulk `supabase functions deploy` must see those pins.
# It contains no secrets (project_id is public, it's in every Supabase URL);
# the link-time credentials live under supabase/.temp/, which stays ignored.

# Generated agent context pack (scripts/context-pack.ts). Derived from local
# agent transcripts and live tenant rows, both of which stay on the laptop,
# and stale within hours anyway: the generator is tracked, the output is not.
# The generator mirrors it into every checkout and writes through a temp file.
docs/CONTEXT-PACK.md
docs/CONTEXT-PACK.md.tmp-*

